Environment variables for cPanel → Setup Node.js App → your app → "Environment variables".
Add each NAME with its value (no quotes). Lines marked (optional) can be skipped.

NODE_ENV                = production
DATABASE_URL            = (Neon connection string, "Pooled connection" off, ends with ?sslmode=require)
APP_BASE_URL            = https://coverageoncall.com
SESSION_SECRET          = (64 random characters — see guide step 4)
CRON_SECRET             = (another 64 random characters)
SETUP_TOKEN             = (another random string; remove after setup)
UPLOAD_DIR              = /home/YOUR_CPANEL_USER/coverageoncall.com/uploads

BRAND_NAME              = CoverageOnCall
BRAND_DOMAIN            = coverageoncall.com
BRAND_SUPPORT_EMAIL     = support@coverageoncall.com
BRAND_TAGLINE           = Licensed coverage for your clinic, on call.   (optional)

STRIPE_SECRET_KEY       = sk_live_...
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET   = whsec_...,whsec_...   (both webhook signing secrets, comma-separated — guide Step 9)
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  = pk_live_...
SENDGRID_API_KEY        = SG....
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY     = AIza...

TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID           = AC...   (optional — without it no text messages are sent)
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN            = ...     (optional)
TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID = MG...   (optional)
ESIGN_TEST_MODE              = true    (until Dropbox Sign is connected: lets people click-sign a test agreement; remove it once the ESIGN_ keys below are set)
ESIGN_API_KEY                = ...     (Dropbox Sign — needed before anyone can finish sign-up)
ESIGN_CLINIC_TEMPLATE_ID     = ...
ESIGN_DOCTOR_TEMPLATE_ID     = ...     (the provider agreement template)
SENTRY_DSN                   = ...     (optional)
